Module 1: Introduction to Pandas
Definition

Pandas is an open-source Python library used for reading, organizing, cleaning, analyzing, manipulating, and storing data in a tabular format.

Why Pandas?
Easy to work with data
Read CSV/Excel files
Clean missing values
Filter and sort data
Perform calculations
Prepare data for Machine Learning
Installation
pip install pandas
Import
import pandas as pd
Module 2: Series
Definition

A Series is a one-dimensional labeled array capable of storing any type of data.

Create Series
import pandas as pd

s = pd.Series([10,20,30,40])
print(s)
Custom Index
s = pd.Series([90,80,70],index=["Math","Science","English"])
Access Data
s[0]
s["Math"]
Module 3: DataFrame
Definition

A DataFrame is a two-dimensional table consisting of rows and columns.

Create DataFrame
data={
    "Name":["Utkarsh","Rahul","Aman"],
    "Age":[20,21,19]
}

df=pd.DataFrame(data)
Display DataFrame
print(df)
Module 4: Reading Files
CSV
df=pd.read_csv("student.csv")
Excel
df=pd.read_excel("student.xlsx")
JSON
df=pd.read_json("student.json")
Module 5: Inspecting Data
First Rows
df.head()
Last Rows
df.tail()
Random Rows
df.sample()
Shape
df.shape
Columns
df.columns
Index
df.index
Data Types
df.dtypes
Information
df.info()
Statistics
df.describe()
Module 6: Selecting Data
Single Column
df["Name"]
Multiple Columns
df[["Name","Age"]]
Row using iloc
df.iloc[0]
Multiple Rows
df.iloc[0:5]
Row using loc
df.loc[0]
Module 7: Filtering Data
Age > 18
df[df["Age"]>18]
Equal Condition
df[df["City"]=="Lucknow"]
Multiple Conditions
df[(df["Age"]>18) & (df["Marks"]>80)]
Module 8: Sorting
Ascending
df.sort_values("Age")
Descending
df.sort_values("Age",ascending=False)
Module 9: Add Column
df["Salary"]=[10000,20000,30000]
Calculate Column
df["Total"]=df["Math"]+df["Science"]
Module 10: Delete Data
Delete Column
df.drop("Age",axis=1)
Delete Row
df.drop(0)
Module 11: Missing Values
Check Missing Values
df.isnull()
Count Missing Values
df.isnull().sum()
Remove Missing Values
df.dropna()
Fill Missing Values
df.fillna(0)
Module 12: Duplicate Values
Find Duplicates
df.duplicated()
Remove Duplicates
df.drop_duplicates()
Module 13: Rename
Rename Column
df.rename(columns={"Age":"Student_Age"})
Module 14: Mathematical Functions
Sum
df["Marks"].sum()
Mean
df["Marks"].mean()
Maximum
df["Marks"].max()
Minimum
df["Marks"].min()
Count
df["Marks"].count()
Median
df["Marks"].median()
Mode
df["Marks"].mode()
Standard Deviation
df["Marks"].std()
Module 15: GroupBy
Average Marks by City
df.groupby("City")["Marks"].mean()
Count Students
df.groupby("City").count()
Module 16: Merge
Merge Two DataFrames
pd.merge(df1,df2,on="ID")
Module 17: Concat
pd.concat([df1,df2])
Module 18: String Functions
Upper
df["Name"].str.upper()
Lower
df["Name"].str.lower()
Replace
df["Name"].str.replace("A","X")
Contains
df["Name"].str.contains("Ut")
Module 19: Date Time
df["Date"]=pd.to_datetime(df["Date"])
Year
df["Date"].dt.year
Month
df["Date"].dt.month
Day
df["Date"].dt.day
Module 20: Apply Function
df["Age"]=df["Age"].apply(lambda x:x+1)
Module 21: Pivot Table
pd.pivot_table(df,index="City",values="Marks",aggfunc="mean")
Module 22: Export Data
CSV
df.to_csv("output.csv",index=False)
Excel
df.to_excel("output.xlsx",index=False)
